---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { books } from '../data/bookshelf';
---

<BaseLayout title="Bookshelf" description="A running list of what I'm reading and have read.">
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <p class="label">Reading</p>
    <h1>Bookshelf</h1>
    <blockquote class="quote">
      “One glance at a book and you hear the voice of another person,
      perhaps someone dead for 1,000 years.{' '}
      <span class="accent">To read is to voyage through time.</span>”
      <cite>— Carl Sagan</cite>
    </blockquote>
    <div class="prose page-desc">
      <p>
        I love reading books. There have been times when I have been
        overcome by a great sorrow, when I could not see the point of life
        and the road ahead seemed to stretch endlessly into darkness, with
        no light at the end of the tunnel. And yet, even then, the thought
        of reading a book felt like that light.
      </p>

      <p>
        The thought that I could open a book and, for a while, experience
        life as someone else—to laugh, to love, to grieve, to wonder—has
        always been deeply comforting to me. To be reminded that there are
        still stories waiting to be lived, even if only through the pages
        of a book, has sometimes been enough to make life feel bearable
        again.
      </p>

      <p>
        Funnily enough, it has always been the sad stories that have
        stayed closest to my heart. Perhaps that is why Kafka’s words
        resonate with me so deeply:
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        “I think we ought to read only the kind of books that wound or
        stab us... A book must be the axe for the frozen sea within us.
        That is my belief.”
      </blockquote>

      <p>
        So here is a list of the books I have read and the ones I am
        reading—not in any particular order, but as an ode to the very
        things that make life livable.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap shelves">
    {
      books.length > 0 ? (
        <ul class="book-list">
          {books.map((b) => (
            <li>
              <span class={`dot ${b.status === 'reading' ? 'dot-reading' : ''}`} aria-hidden="true" />
              <span class="book-content">
                <span class="book-title">{b.title}</span>
                <span class="book-author">{b.author}</span>
                {b.note && <span class="book-note">{b.note}</span>}
              </span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      ) : (
        <p class="empty">Nothing on the shelf yet.</p>
      )
    }
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head {
    padding-top: var(--space-7);
  }

  .quote {
    margin: var(--space-4) 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: none;
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 2.6vw, 1.7rem);
    line-height: 1.45;
    color: var(--color-fg);
    max-width: 46ch;
  }

  .quote cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--color-fg-faint);
  }

  .quote .accent {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .page-desc {
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
  }

  .shelves {
    padding-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }

  .book-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .book-list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 12px 1fr;
    column-gap: 0.55em;
    padding-block: 0.55rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .dot {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    width: 5px;
    height: 5px;
    margin-top: 0.55em;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-fg-faint);
    justify-self: center;
  }

  .book-content {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.1em 0.5em;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
  }

  .dot-reading {
    background: transparent;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-fg-faint);
  }

  .book-title {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-fg);
  }

  .book-author {
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .book-author::before {
    content: '— ';
  }

  .book-note {
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-fg-faint);
    width: 100%;
  }

  .empty {
    color: var(--color-fg-muted);
  }
</style>
